{"raw": {"https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/57646": {"title": "Swim Instructor", "description": "Swim Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/95718": {"title": "Slate and Student Success Data Administrator", "description": "Slate and Student Success Data Administrator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Slate and Student Success Data Administrator Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $80,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Staff Apply Description About the Opportunity The\u00a0Slate & Student Success Data Administrator\u00a0serves as the primary system administrator and functional expert for the\u00a0College\u2019s\u00a0Slate Student Success CRM instance, while also leading data projects that support student retention and success initiatives. This position\u00a0is responsible for\u00a0the configuration, maintenance,\u00a0and\u00a0ongoing optimization of Slate to support\u00a0the needs of Student Success & Engagement and other College partners. This position will work with\u00a0College\u00a0partners to\u00a0develop predictive retention models\u00a0to support the needs of the Crest-to-Career\u00a0project, and\u00a0works\u00a0closely with\u00a0colleagues in Enrollment Management and\u00a0Academic Affairs\u00a0on Slate projects to\u00a0align system capabilities and data initiatives with institutional goals and to ensure data-driven decision making that improves student outcomes. The\u00a0Crest to Career\u00a0project is a 5-year project\u00a0support\u00a0by a federal\u00a0Title III Strengthening Institutions Program grant.\u00a0By\u00a0supporting\u00a0further Slate implementation and the\u00a0development of data analysis tools, this position strengthens the College\u2019s enrollment and fiscal stability through improved data access, information sharing, and data decision-making. Key Responsibilities Slate system\u00a0administration (75%) Serve as the primary Slate Captain for the Slate Student Success instance,\u00a0maintaining\u00a0overall system configuration and ensuring platform health. Build and\u00a0maintain\u00a0forms, populations, queries, rules, dashboards, reports, and portals within Slate. Design and implement automated workflows, such as those to\u00a0support\u00a0advising\u00a0outreach, case management, and student communications.\u00a0Apply process improvement techniques to\u00a0identify\u00a0manual workflows that can be replaced with sustainable, system-driven solutions. Partner with Student Success, Academic Advising, Financial Aid, Residential Life, and other campus units to translate operational needs into scalable Slate configurations and data solutions. Design and deliver training programs for Slate users across student success units, including onboarding sessions, user guides, and workshops. Act as the primary point of contact for day-to-day Slate support requests from functional users, investigating\u00a0issues\u00a0and implementing resolutions. Manage user access, roles, and permissions in compliance with institutional data governance and FERPA requirements. Oversee lifecycle planning for platform upgrades, new modules, and long-term system evolution. Monitor system performance and troubleshoot technical and functional issues, implementing\u00a0solutions\u00a0or escalating as\u00a0appropriate. Document all system configurations, processes, and procedural changes in an\u00a0administrative manual. Stay current on Slate releases, new features, and community best practices, assessing their relevance and value to the institution. Coordinate with IT colleagues to\u00a0maintain\u00a0and troubleshoot integrations between Slate and Jenzabar and other enterprise systems. Participate in committees and related working groups as assigned to ensure consistent data standards and stewardship across systems. Build and\u00a0maintain\u00a0operational reports and dashboards that\u00a0provide\u00a0actionable insights to student success leadership and front-line staff. Champion data quality across the Slate Student Success instance,\u00a0establishing\u00a0and enforcing data entry standards and validation rules. Predictive Analytics & Data Projects (25%) Partner with Information Technology, the Registrar\u2019s Office, and Institutional Research\u00a0to develop, test, and refine predictive models for student retention using data from Jenzabar and the Slate Student Success instance. Coordinate the extraction, integration, and validation of data feeds between Jenzabar and Slate to support predictive modeling. Translate model outputs (e.g., risk scores, retention indicators) into actionable Slate workflows, populations, and communication triggers for advisors and student success staff. Collaborate with stakeholders to\u00a0identify\u00a0new data sources and variables that could improve the accuracy and usefulness of predictive models. Monitor and report on the performance and impact of predictive models, recommending refinements based on outcomes data. Serve as a liaison between Student Success, IT, and Institutional Research on data projects related to retention, persistence, and graduation analytics. Qualifications What We're Looking For Qualifications Education Bachelor\u2019s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Management Information Systems, Statistics, Higher Education, or\u00a0a related field.\u00a0Equivalent\u00a0combination of education and experience will be considered. Experience Minimum of 3\u20134 years of hands-on experience\u00a0building or\u00a0administering\u00a0Technolutions\u00a0Slate or a comparable CRM platform, including building queries, forms, workflows, and portals. Experience working in or closely with a higher education\u00a0student\u00a0success, academic advising, or student affairs environment. Demonstrated experience with requirements gathering, business process analysis, and translating stakeholder needs into system solutions. Experience with data analysis, reporting tools, and relational database concepts, including working with ERP data (Jenzabar experience preferred). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong understanding of Slate CRM administrative functions, including populations, rules, forms, queries, reports, and communication workflows. Familiarity with ERP integration processes (data imports/exports, sync troubleshooting), ideally with Jenzabar. Working knowledge of statistical or predictive modeling concepts as applied to student retention (e.g., regression, risk scoring), or strong aptitude and willingness to develop this skill set. Knowledge of FERPA and applicable data security and privacy standards for student information. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously in a deadline-oriented environment with strong attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build collaborative relationships across technical and non-technical audiences. Self-motivated and proactive in\u00a0identifying\u00a0opportunities to improve system performance and user experience. Commitment to equity, inclusion, and serving students from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience specifically with Slate for Student Success (as distinct from Slate for Admissions). Direct experience with Jenzabar as a data source for reporting or analytics. Hands-on experience building or supporting predictive retention models or similar institutional analytics projects. Familiarity with statistical software or languages for data analysis and modeling. Familiarity with HTML, CSS, Liquid Markup, JavaScript, or SQL for advanced Slate customization. Experience with Business Intelligence platforms such as Cognos, Power BI, or Tableau. What We Offer Be Part of a Purpose-Driven Community:\u00a0Your work will help create a safe, beautiful, and inviting campus that supports learning, leadership, and civic engagement. Work in a Unique Setting:\u00a0Our campus is a certified arboretum, offering the opportunity to care for a diverse collection of trees and green spaces in a historic and inspiring environment. Comprehensive Benefits:\u00a0In addition to health, dental, vision, and retirement benefits, we offer a unique tuition benefit for employees and their families. While Cedar Crest is a women\u2019s college, men can access certain classes on campus and others at partner institutions, making this benefit flexible and valuable for all. Support for Growth:\u00a0We encourage professional development and\u00a0provide training opportunities for team members. Campus Culture:\u00a0Cedar Crest is a place where your story is valued.\u00a0We see you, and\u00a0we\u2019re\u00a0here to help you shape your future. How to Apply For full consideration , please\u00a0submit: Current resume Cover letter highlighting your relevant experience Contact information for three professional references Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/87597": {"title": "Senior Accountant", "description": "Senior Accountant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Accountant Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,000.00 - $75,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Staff Apply Description About the Opportunity The Senior Accountant\u00a0maintains\u00a0the College\u2019s general ledger and accounting records and\u00a0is responsible for\u00a0ensuring the accuracy, validity, and completeness of all financial transactions.\u00a0 Prepares reconciliations of the general ledger account balances to the supporting subsidiary ledgers and other source records.\u00a0Assists\u00a0with the month and year-end close processes and with the preparation of schedules necessary for the year-end audit. The Senior Accountant also processes all requests for payment and generates disbursements on a weekly schedule, researches and resolves A/P problems on\u00a0a timely\u00a0basis and\u00a0posts all procurement card expense reports. Key Responsibilities Prepare necessary journal entries for the month and year-end close process. Verify the accuracy,\u00a0validity\u00a0and completeness of the entries received from other departments to the general ledger.\u00a0\u00a0Identify\u00a0problems and potential solutions to ensure\u00a0accurate\u00a0and\u00a0timely\u00a0financial reporting. Prepare and run customized reports for the College Community as needed to\u00a0facilitate\u00a0budgeting and planning. Reconcile the bank statements, outstanding\u00a0checks\u00a0and general ledger accounts on a monthly basis.\u00a0\u00a0Make corresponding journal entries to record activity or to correct any discrepancies found. Perform general ledger recalculations and maintenance within the accounting software, which includes account and business officer set up. Assist\u00a0with preparation of annual\u00a0tax exempt\u00a0returns, Form\u00a0990\u00a0and Form 990-T. Process invoices for payment through check, ACH, Wire, or Credit Card. Assist\u00a0with inquires related to payables, vendor disputes, etc. Accurately complete all College 1099\u2019s on an annual basis. Reconcile and review Procurement card\u00a0purchases\u00a0and expense reports. Alert leadership to any questionable payment requests or documentation from various departments. Ensure that invoices at year-end are put in proper fiscal year and provide copies of invoices for necessary accruals. Complete and distribute invoices for applicable funds,\u00a0mainly restricted\u00a0grant accounts. Maintain, review, and reconcile all endowed funds\u00a0on a monthly basis. Maintain the fixed asset software and spreadsheets, which includes\u00a0the capitalization\u00a0and depreciation of assets. Assist the Controller with the month and year-end close of the general ledger, which includes the preparation of\u00a0director\u2019s\u00a0report packages and summary level reports for management and reviewing departmental balances for overages or discrepancies. Process month end reports from software for month end reconciliations. Monitor prepaid expenses/accruals\u00a0on a monthly basis\u00a0for necessary adjustments and update spreadsheets which track these expenses. Prepare various schedules and financial reports as\u00a0required\u00a0to support the College\u2019s independent auditors.\u00a0Assist\u00a0in the completion of the annual financial statement, A-133,\u00a0IAG\u00a0and other audits. Develop and\u00a0maintain\u00a0other analytical spreadsheets as\u00a0required. Assist\u00a0in the coordination of annual budget requests,\u00a0upload of\u00a0the final budgets to the accounting\u00a0software\u00a0and generate summary reports for review and analysis. Completion of Finance Office surveys and Key Operating Data Annual Report. Ensure the College\u2019s accounting policies and practices are\u00a0in accordance with\u00a0GAAP. Prepare and scan all\u00a0appropriate documentation\u00a0in applicable imaging software. Maintain file copies of all supporting financial records and issued reports. Maintain file copies of grants, other external funding agreements, and contracts to which the College is a party. Other duties as assigned by leadership. Qualifications What We're Looking For Education and Training Bachelor's degree in accounting\u00a0(or equivalent experience)\u00a0required\u00a0with knowledge of GAAP. Not-for-Profit/Higher Education experience preferred. Advanced spreadsheet skills on Microsoft Excel,\u00a0Access\u00a0and\u00a0Powersoft\u00a0InfoMaker. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Working knowledge of not-for-profit accounting standards and financial issues pertinent to higher education institutions. Excellent organizational and time management skills, including the ability to successfully manage multiple tasks simultaneously and prioritize effectively to meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail with a commitment to accuracy and efficiency. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both verbal and written. Able to react and adapt to changing situations appropriately. Strong commitment to and focus on customer service. Commitment to confidentiality and integrity of systems and processes. Physical Requirements and Working Conditions Able to communicate both verbally and in writing with or without the use of auxiliary devices. Able to sit up to 90% of the working day and have sufficient dexterity to\u00a0operate\u00a0personal\u00a0computer, printer, and other office equipment. Able and available to work outside of normal business hours to meet College obligations. What We Offer Be Part of a Purpose-Driven Community:\u202fYour work will help create a safe, beautiful, and inviting campus that supports learning, leadership, and civic engagement. Work in a Unique Setting:\u202fOur campus is a certified arboretum, offering the opportunity to care for a diverse collection of trees and green spaces in a historic and inspiring environment. Comprehensive Benefits:\u202fIn addition to health, dental, vision, and retirement benefits, we offer a unique tuition benefit for employees and their families. While Cedar Crest is a women\u2019s college, men can access certain classes on campus and others at partner institutions, making this benefit flexible and valuable for all. Support for Growth:\u202fWe encourage professional development and\u202fprovide training opportunities for team members. Campus Culture:\u202fCedar Crest is a place where your story is valued.\u202fWe see you, and\u202fwe\u2019re\u202fhere to help you shape your future. How to Apply Pease\u202fsubmit: Current resume Cover letter highlighting your relevant experience Contact information for three professional references Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/95748": {"title": "Occupational Therapy Faculty", "description": "Occupational Therapy Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Occupational Therapy Faculty Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $80,000.00 Position Type Full Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Faculty Apply Description Cedar Crest College invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Occupational Therapy at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor The Occupational Therapy Doctorate (OTD) program in the Health Sciences Department at Cedar Crest College invites applications for a 12-month, in-person faculty position. The program is seeking a motivated and innovative individual to join a collaborative, clinically focused, and student-centered team. The OTD program is committed to fostering a diverse faculty team with a global perspective. Our mission is to cultivate an inclusive, transformative learning environment to prepare students for the evolving demands of healthcare. Key Responsibilities: \u00b7 Teaching graduate-level courses in an entry-level occupational therapy doctorate program. \u00b7 Advising and mentoring graduate students, including guiding student-practitioner evidence-based projects and doctoral capstone projects. \u00b7 Ongoing evaluation and development of curriculum to align with program goals and accreditation standards. \u00b7 Conducting and disseminating scholarly work in accordance with the Boyer Model of Scholarship. \u00b7 Supporting admissions processes and engaging in departmental and college-wide service. \u00b7 Maintaining clinical expertise through optional weekly clinical release time. Qualifications Desired Areas of Expertise: All qualified candidates are welcome to apply and those with psychosocial experience are strongly encouraged to apply. Qualifications: \u00b7 Doctorate degree (e.g., PhD, EdD, DSc, DrPH, OTD). \u00b7 Certification by the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). \u00b7 Active Pennsylvania OT licensure or eligibility for licensure in Pennsylvania. \u00b7 A minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. \u00b7 Academic experience, including knowledge of OT curriculum development and accreditation processes, is preferred. \u00b7 Excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. \u00b7 Strong organizational, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. Additional Application Requirements: Applicants are asked to submit: 1. A letter of interest. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. A statement of teaching philosophy. 4. Three letters of reference. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/57614": {"title": "Lifeguard", "description": "Lifeguard You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Lifeguard Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $13.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time Category Staff Apply Description Rodale Aquatic Center (RAC), located on the campus of Cedar Crest College, is seeking qualified Lifeguards to join our busy center on a part time basis.\u00a0 RAC is dedicated to fostering civic health and wellness by providing educational opportunities to the campus and the larger community, alone and in cooperation with other organizations that enhance the development of the mind, body and spirit through a large offering of instruction and fitness classes. These part-time positions are flexible, between 10 \u2013 25 hours per week. Qualifications Part-time afternoon and evening hours with the flexibility to extend hours throughout the day, evening and weekends.\u00a0 Current lifeguarding certification required. Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), resume, three references. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/113892": {"title": "Assistant Director of Learning Support Services", "description": "Assistant Director of Learning Support Services You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/108883": {"title": "Administrative Assistant for Financial Aid", "description": "Administrative Assistant for Financial Aid You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/80301": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Adjunct Apply Position Description The School of Nursing\u00a0at Cedar Crest College is seeking adjunct faculty with experience in medical-surgical nursing to join our dynamic team focused on educating future nurse leaders with quality instruction in state of the art facilities with Simulation Center.\u00a0 Adjunct faculty will serve as clinical instructors for the fall 2021 semester, primarily on weekends. Qualifications Candidates for adjunct faculty must have an MSN (or be currently enrolled in and pursuing an MSN). Experience in the medical-surgical nursing required. Experience teaching in a college environment strongly preferred. Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and three letters of reference. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/82055": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Math", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Math You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Math Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Adjunct Apply Description The Department of Mathematics at Cedar Crest College invites applications for adjunct faculty to teach courses in the areas of Probability and Statistics, Precalculus, and College Mathematics.\u00a0 Candidates must be available to teach courses between the hours of 8am and noon. Qualifications Qualified candidates must possess a Master\u2019s degree or Ph.D. in mathematics or a related field.\u00a0Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level is required. Application Instructions A complete application includes a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three letters of reference.\u00a0 At least one of the letters of reference must address teaching excellence.\u00a0\u00a0 Please indicate preferred courses of instruction when submitting materials.\u00a0 Responses will be sent only to those under consideration. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/80448": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry & Physics", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry & Physics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry & Physics Apply Apply Description The Department of Chemical, Physical, & Forensic Sciences at Cedar Crest College is seeking adjunct faculty to teach Introductory Chemistry laboratory and Physics courses (all taught on campus, in person). We seek to recruit faculty prepared to teach our students, engage their curiosity, and inspire their persistence. Qualifications Adjunct faculty should have a minimum of a Master\u2019s Degree in chemistry, or closely related field, and experience teaching at the undergraduate college level is strongly preferred. Applicants will be expected to demonstrate competency in using Canvas as a learning management system and guide students to complete experiments safely in the chemistry laboratory setting. Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and three letters of reference.\u00a0Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. 