ergraduate level introduces the student to theories in art therapy and develops the student\u2019s technical skills in multiple studio mediums. The Art Therapy undergraduate major prepares students to pursue graduate studies in Art Therapy. Qualifications Applicants from Pennsylvania and New Jersey are welcome to apply.\u202f Adjunct faculty are required to hold a Master\u2019s Degree in Art Therapy, be credentialed as an ATR-BC, and to have a minimum of three years professional experience. Prior experience teaching at the college level is strongly preferred. Courses are taught on campus Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and three letters of reference. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/110765": {"title": "Adjunct - Biological Sciences", "description": "Adjunct - Biological Sciences You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct - Biological Sciences Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Adjunct Apply Description Position Description The Department of Biological Sciences at Cedar Crest College is seeking adjunct faculty to teach Anatomy & Physiology I&II laboratories (all taught on campus, in person) in the spring of 2027, with a potential for future appointments in summer and fall.\u00a0 Adjuncts for this course are provided in person and online teaching materials, along with laboratory material set up by a lab coordinator to ensure consistency across lab sections. Candidates must be available to teach labs at times that may include 8-11AM, 1-4PM, 4-7PM, and/or 7-10PM. We also seek to establish an adjunct pool that could teach in future spring, summer, and fall semesters with expertise that could cover Clinical Microbiology labs for nursing students, Introductory Biology labs for science majors, and General Biology courses for non-majors, and encourage anyone interested in teaching these courses to apply. When you apply, please indicate which of these biology courses you are interested in teaching. All applicants should have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level.\u00a0 We seek to recruit faculty prepared to teach our students, engage their curiosity, and inspire their persistence. Qualifications Qualifications Adjunct faculty should have a minimum of a Master's degree or higher in Anatomy, Anatomical Sciences, Biology or Biological field, Kinesiology, Medicine, Nursing, Physician Associate Studies, Physical Therapy, Occupational Therapy, or a closely related field. Demonstrated experience teaching at the undergraduate college level is strongly preferred. Applicants will be expected to demonstrate competency in using Canvas as a learning management system and guide students to complete experiments safely in the laboratory setting. Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy (if available), and three letters of reference.\u00a0 At least one of the letters of reference must address teaching excellence.\u00a0 Responses will be sent only to those under consideration. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. \u201c0\u201d on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}}, "rows": {"https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/57646": {"school_id": 1125, "posting_url": "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/57646", "job_title_in_post": "Swim Instructor", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Swim", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/95718": {"school_id": 1125, "posting_url": "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/95718", "job_title_in_post": "Slate and Student Success Data Administrator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.paycomonline.net